  "borough": "Islington",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed works, including the excavation of the lightwell, internalisation of the vaults, enlargement of the canopy and reconfiguration of rainwater goods would result in harm to the special architectural and historic interest of the Grade II Listed Building. The application lacks sufficient structural and waterproofing details, and the interventions are contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policies D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Policies PLAN1, DH1 and DH2 of the Islington Strategic and Development Management Policies (2023) as well as the guidance contained within Islington’s Urban Design Guide (2017), Duncan Terrace/Colebrooke Row Conservation Area Design Guide (2002) and Islington’s Basement Development SPD (2016). It is not considered that there is sufficient public benefit to outweigh the less than substantial harm to the significance of the heritage asset."
